# Use-case 06 gap 1 (claim C3) -- FIXED 2026-08-26 by the
# template-clone isolation change (ADR-005): each generated child is a
# FULL per-destination instance (the deep `dup` clone / instanceClone),
# so key() inside a close()d pack template resolves per child.
# Historically close() around the template was sufficient on its own
# to cross-wire: the base func clone shared its argument Vals, key()
# evaluated once in the one shared inner map, and every child got the
# FIRST child's key, exit 0. The garbled $.deploy.NaN.p path on
# partial overrides is gone with it (an extra key now refuses cleanly
# with [aontu/closed] at the child's real path).
# Pinned in both engines: test/spec/gen-close.tsv
# close-template-keys-per-child, close-template-key-pref-override,
# close-template-key-refuses-extra.
# expected: {"deploy":{"auth":{"name":"auth"},"web":{"name":"web"}},...} exit 0
# actual:   {"deploy":{"auth":{"name":"auth"},"web":{"name":"web"}},...} exit 0
names: [web, auth]
deploy: pack($.names, close({ name: key() }))
